Idle Farmer v2 (ssh-farm)
=========================

Third-party software distributed in the published container image
(ghcr.io/mynameis-nigel/ssh-farm).

ssh-farm itself is MIT-licensed; see LICENSE. The entries below cover software
that is redistributed *inside the image*, rather than depended on as source.


Litestream
----------

  Version:  0.5.17  (pinned in build/litestream/go.mod)
  Source:   https://github.com/benbjohnson/litestream
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0
            https://github.com/benbjohnson/litestream/blob/main/LICENSE

Used as the replication process that supervises the game binary. It is a
separate program run as the container's supervising process, not linked into
this program's code.

Compiled from upstream source at v0.5.17 by the Dockerfile's litestream
stage, rather than copied from the prebuilt litestream/litestream image —
see that stage for why. No source file is patched or vendored. What does
differ from an upstream build: it is compiled with this repository's Go
toolchain, and three transitive module dependencies are raised above the
versions v0.5.17 pins, to versions carrying fixes for advisories the release
scan fails on. Those three are named, with the advisory each answers, in
build/litestream/go.mod.

Apache-2.0 section 4 requires this attribution to travel with the binary,
which is why this file exists even though none of this repository's own code
is Apache-licensed. Section 4(b) asks that modified files carry notice of the
change; no file of litestream's is modified, and the paragraph above states
the build deltas so the distinction is on the record either way.

Libraries linked into the litestream binary
-------------------------------------------

Building litestream here rather than shipping someone else's build makes this
repository the one combining litestream's dependency tree into a redistributed
binary, so those licences are in scope where previously they sat behind an
opaque upstream artefact. That tree is largely Apache-2.0 — the AWS and Azure
SDKs, gRPC, OpenTelemetry and the Prometheus client among them — alongside
MIT and BSD-3-Clause modules.

The full list, with exact versions and checksums, is build/litestream/go.mod
and build/litestream/go.sum; each module's own repository carries its licence
text and any NOTICE of its own. They are enumerated there rather than copied
here for the same reason the base image is not enumerated below: a list
maintained by hand goes stale, and the generated one is already in the tree
and machine-checkable against the image's SBOM.


Go module dependencies
----------------------

This section covers the game's own dependencies — the root go.mod. Every one
is permissive (MIT or BSD-3-Clause) and is compiled into the binary rather
than redistributed as a separate work. See go.mod for the list, and each
module's own repository for its licence text.

litestream's dependencies are a separate tree with a separate licence mix;
they are covered above, under the litestream entry.


Base image
----------

The runtime is alpine:3.22 plus ca-certificates. Packages arriving with the
base image are covered by their own licences as published by Alpine Linux
(https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org) and are not enumerated here — the same scope
boundary ssh-chess's NOTICE draws.
